text:
Rae Kim: Quick sync from today's console review: we still have inconsistencies in compact rows, modal padding, and toast anchoring. Need token decisions.
Omar Vasquez: I prototyped two token sets: "compact-lean" and "compact-comfort". Lean uses --compact-gap:4px and icon 14px, comfort uses 6px and 16px.
Sofia Park: I'm leaning toward comfort for dashboards with dense data; lean feels brittle on touch. But we can offer lean for read-only lists.
Liam Grant: Accessibility note: visual icon can be 14px/16px but hit area must remain 44px. Document visual vs hit tokens.
Rae Kim: Agreed. Proposed canonical tokens: 
```
--compact-gap: 6px;
--compact-icon-size: 16px;
--icon-hit-area: 44px;
--table-row-compact-gap: 6px;
--modal-header-padding-compact: 12px;
--toast-anchor-offset: calc(var(--pinned-toolbar-height) + 8px);
```
Omar Vasquez: Also suggest behavior: default toasts sit under modals; actionable toasts prefer mounting into modal header when modal open. Fallback: mark with data-toast-priority\="high\" to promote above overlay.
Sofia Park: Copy nit: replace terse toasts ("Saved") with context: "Settings saved  changes applied". I'll add i18n keys.
Liam Grant: Small CSS snippet for implementation: 
```
.icon-compact { width: var(--compact-icon-size); height: var(--compact-icon-size); }
.icon-compact__hit { padding: calc((var(--icon-hit-area) - var(--compact-icon-size)) / 2); }
.toast { top: var(--toast-anchor-offset); }
.surface--modal .toast:not([data-toast-priority\="high\"]) { aria-hidden: true; }
```
Rae Kim: Action items: Omar add tokens + playground variants (lean/comfort), Sofia update copy + i18n, Liam add accessibility docs on hit areas and focus behavior. I'll track in the PR. :memo:
design-bot: Draft tokens file created: design/tokens/compact-layout.yml (preview).
Omar Vasquez: I'll include examples for mounting toast into modal header and visual tests for narrow viewports.
Sofia Park: Also adding a quick lint rule: icon-only buttons must include aria-label. QA flagged two missing in the compact story.
Liam Grant: I'll run contrast and focus-ring regression tests after the PR lands.
Rae Kim: Thanks all. If we land this today we can stabilize the compact variant for the minor release. :rocket:
